The standard used to assess magnitude is less than 20%, this figure may vary across different industries. As all unsolvable issues have a magnitude of less than 20%, they will be disregarded as they will not have a significant impact on the results of the analysis.

#### Step 4: Augment the data

At this stage, the quality and flexibility of the data will be improved by creating new columns as additional indicators, which will make the analysis easier later on.

Data is added by:
- Extracting data from the PURCHASE_TS column and creating new columns:
  - PURCHASE_YEAR: the year the transaction took place
  - PURCHASE_MONTH: the month in which the transaction took place
- Performing calculations on the PURCHASE_TS and SHIP_TS columns to obtain new data.
  - TIME_TO_SHIP: the time interval before the goods were dispatched
- Adding a new column so that the customer’s country of origin, as recorded in the COUNTRY_CODE column, can be clearly identified.
  - REGION: the name of the customer’s country of origin

